{
  "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
  "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
  "records": [
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0000-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 3,
        "start": 3
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: Justice Stevens, and may it please the Court: This case, like the Totten case almost 130 years ago, is at bottom an effort by alleged spies to obtain additional compensation for services rendered."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice O'Connor",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0000-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 4,
        "start": 4
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE O'CONNOR: Would the Government be without any recourse if it was an alleged espionage agent?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioners (Mr. Clement)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0000-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "MR. CLEMENT: If I understand your hypothetical, Justice Stevens, I think that individual would be treated as an espionage agent if it's just somebody for sort of a one-off assignment."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Kennedy",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0000-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 5,
        "start": 5
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE KENNEDY: I -- I'd like your help on this. Your interpretation of Totten -- does it say that there is just no actionable contract, or does it say there's no jurisdictions like political question?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0000",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 18,
        "start": 18
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "And I would analogize it to this Court's decision in Snepp where the Court adopted a constructive trust arrangement. The Court adopted that arrangement where -- where an employee who violated a -- a prepublication review agreement had to turn over all the proceeds to the Government."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Stevens",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0001",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 19,
        "start": 19
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I don't remember whether the briefs discuss it or not, but is there a statute that prohibits the disclosure of secret agents like this and does that -- if so, does that have any relevance to this case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0003",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 22,
        "start": 22
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But you're not making that statement with respect to anything that's classified. There was something in your brief, reply brief, at 18 and 19 in which you -- you cite Reynolds and you say the proper response to classified information in civil litigation is to disregard the classified information, not to order partial disclosure to court personnel. Are -\u00ad are you saying then in all of civil litigation if information is classified, then it's just out of the case?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Clement",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0007",
      "kind": "fact",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 26,
        "start": 26
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "There this Court applied Totten to not force the Navy to produce an environmental impact statement even though there were regulations on the book -- and the concurring Justices focused on those regulations -- where the Department of Defense said we do produce an environmental impact statement even if it's classified."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Burman",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 27,
        "start": 27
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We allege that they were coerced into that relationship, but we do -\u00ad"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0012",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 33,
        "start": 33
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "But if the question comes up, you're going to have to disclose the identity. I mean, if -- if it is controverted whether indeed you're -- you're a spy or not, then what do you do? Do you say, well, we'll -- we'll do it in camera?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Burman",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0001-0013",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 34,
        "start": 34
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We do not believe that we have to have -- that we have to disclose anything to the district court to have standing as Does to seek a fair procedure within the CIA."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0000",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 35,
        "start": 35
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "argued on pages 37 to 40 of their brief for exactly the same interpretation of Totten that they are arguing now."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Burman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0001",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "What we still have, though, is a claim to a fair, internal agency procedure."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Ginsburg",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0002",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 36,
        "start": 36
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE GINSBURG: Attached to what? I mean, you can -- a fair procedure leading nowhere is not a claim."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Mr. Burman (Petitioner)",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0003",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 39,
        "start": 39
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We also believe there is a liberty interest. These people came to the U.S. in danger."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0005",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have standing to make a claim for fair procedures."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0006",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 40,
        "start": 40
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "We have sought preapproval of every single filing."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0004",
      "kind": "stated_consequence",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "I mean, they say, look, frankly we'd rather reveal the names of one or two spies than we would like to reveal our procedures for dealing with the spies we bring into the United States. It will take someone who reads those about 15 minutes with a computer to locate 400 resettled spies. That will be a terrible disaster."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Justice Scalia",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0007",
      "kind": "justice_question",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 42,
        "start": 42
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "JUSTICE SCALIA: Do these regulations just set forth a procedure or do they set forth some substantive entitlement?"
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Petitioner",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 1.0,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0002-0008",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 43,
        "start": 43
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "process for applying that standard must remain internal to the CIA. The Does share the interest in protecting their identity and the identities of others like them."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Plaintiff",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 0.9,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0003-0000",
      "kind": "party_argument",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "uncertain",
      "text": "litigation, and I would ask you to look at those pleadings. The complaint is replete with references to the espionage relationship, and the complaint itself cites Totten or the Totten doctrine no less than seven times. I would suggest that if this claim is not Totten-barred, then no claim is. With that, I'd ask the court below be reversed."
    },
    {
      "attribution": "Court",
      "case_id": "2004-03-1395",
      "confidence": 0.95,
      "document_hash": "8d3225a3cdb5f5c53fa8f24a60cd587f6fb5d0526fccd58fa448ebacb236b9b8",
      "evidence_id": "ev-8d3225a3cdb5-0003-0001",
      "kind": "procedural_event",
      "opinion_part": null,
      "pages": {
        "end": 52,
        "start": 52
      },
      "schema_version": "1.0.0",
      "status": "supported",
      "text": "The case is submitted. (Whereupon, at 12:01 p.m., the case in the above-entitled matter was submitted.)"
    }
  ],
  "schema_version": "1.0.0"
}
